                    "text": "The real issue isn\u2019t funding\u2014it\u2019s bureaucratic bloat. The One Big Beautiful Bill Act (H.R. 1) aims to redirect $1.6T in cuts, but current provisions let pharma middlemen and Medicaid consultants siphon billions.\n\nRural hospitals get crushed by red tape, not lack of cash. Example: 83% of rural facilities drowning in negative margins pre-cuts.\n\nSolution? Slash the $200B in annual Medicaid overpayments to insurers and PBMs instead of gutting care. Reform the waste, fund the frontline.",
